Cell["\<\
Don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t take into account the result. What is important, that \
\[DoubleStruckE][1] element is the first element of commuting blades. So it \
was selected. If the blade we want were not the first one, then we simply \
counted it number in the list of blades which square to 1 and repeated the \
calculation. In the next step we note, that when \[DoubleStruckE][1] was \
selected, the requested element \[DoubleStruckE][2,3,4,5] was in 17-th \
position of blades which commute with \[DoubleStruckE][1], So repeat \
calculations with\
\>", "Text",
